{"search_note":"I did not find a public internal dashboard or party-whip record that shows how tightly the Marcos coalition was managed month by month.

The evidence is strongest for presidency-centered bureaucracy and security coordination. It is weaker for durable party discipline, because the ruling bloc still looks family- and alliance-driven rather than institutionally party-based.

The main unresolved question is whether the same mobilization would hold without Marcos’s personal direction.","evidence":[{"title":"SONA highlights whole-of-government effort to achieve food security, inclusive economic growth - NEDA","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office / NEDA","date":"2024-07-23","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/sona-highlights-whole-of-government-effort-to-achieve-food-security-inclusive-economic-growth-neda/","summary":"Marcos’s SONA was explicitly framed as a whole-of-government implementation push for the Philippine Development Plan 2023-2028, showing coordinated mobilization of the state behind a named program.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","8B.1","7B.5"]},{"title":"PBBM issues EO No. 52 institutionalizing and expanding DSWD's Pag-Abot Program","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office via PIA","date":"2024-01-22","url":"https://mirror.pia.gov.ph/press-releases/2024/01/22/pbbm-issues-eo-no-52-institutionalizing-and-expanding-dswds-pag-abot-program-for-street-dwellers-other-poor-and-vulnerable-individuals","summary":"EO 52 created an inter-agency structure, monitoring system, and reporting cadence for Pag-Abot, which is evidence of bureaucratic mobilization rather than ad hoc patronage.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.9"]},{"title":"PBBM adopts DICT’s National Cybersecurity Plan 2023-2028","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-04-06","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-adopts-dicts-national-cybersecurity-plan-2023-2028/","summary":"EO 58 converted the cybersecurity plan into a whole-of-nation roadmap and ordered agencies and LGUs to implement, monitor, and report, showing real apparatus mobilization.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.8","7B.9"]},{"title":"PBBM reorganizes Inter-Agency Task Force on Zero Hunger","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-08-09","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-reorganizes-inter-agency-task-force-on-zero-hunger/","summary":"Marcos reshuffled the zero-hunger task force to broaden membership and ensure continued implementation, showing the use of a formal coordination mechanism to push the food-security program.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.5"]},{"title":"PBBM sets streamlined permitting for PH infra flagship projects","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-05-04","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-sets-streamlined-permitting-for-ph-infra-flagship-projects/","summary":"EO 59 directed national agencies and LGUs to streamline permits for infrastructure flagship projects, a concrete example of mobilizing bureaucracy toward execution speed.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2"]},{"title":"PBBM signs laws on streamlining procurement, combatting online scams","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-07-20","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-signs-laws-on-streamlining-procurement-combatting-online-scams/","summary":"Procurement reform standardized forms and institutionalized e-procurement, turning the state’s purchasing machinery into a more centrally directed delivery tool.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"PBBM orders agencies to help COS, JO workers get permanent positions in government","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-04-25","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-orders-agencies-to-help-cos-jo-workers-get-permanent-positions-in-government/","summary":"Marcos used executive direction to push agencies to regularize long-serving workers through qualification and training, which is direct administrative mobilization.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.9"]},{"title":"PBBM stands by suspension of 139 NFA officials","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-03-06","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-stands-by-suspension-of-139-nfa-officials/","summary":"Marcos backed enforcement against anomalous rice-sales officials, showing that the bureaucracy could be disciplined and redirected when it misfired.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"PBBM refutes alleged loophole in EO 74, reiterates POGO ban in all forms","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-11-11","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-refutes-alleged-loophole-in-eo-74-reiterates-pogo-ban-in-all-forms/","summary":"Marcos closed off loophole arguments around the POGO ban, which is evidence of enforcement follow-through against a politically sensitive rent stream.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"PBBM calls for comprehensive national flood-control plan to protect communities, production areas","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-07-26","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/pbbm-calls-for-comprehensive-national-flood-control-plan-to-protect-communities-production-areas/","summary":"Marcos used the flood crisis to mobilize agencies around a national mitigation plan and swift assistance, showing state apparatus activation around a priority.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.5"]},{"title":"Marcos’s economic managers publicly set out macro strategy in forum","publisher":"Philippine News Agency","date":"2024-07-08","url":"https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1228524","summary":"The economic team coordinated publicly across NEDA, BSP, DBM, Treasury, and the investment office, which is good evidence of technocratic mobilization behind the chosen macro program.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.5"]},{"title":"Marcos-Romualdez parties forge political alliance","publisher":"BusinessWorld Online","date":"2024-05-08","url":"https://www.bworldonline.com/the-nation/2024/05/08/593686/marcos-romualdez-parties-forge-political-alliance/","summary":"The Marcos and Romualdez parties formed a formal alliance for the 2025 midterms, showing active coalition building around the ruling network.","question_ids":["8B.3","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"PBBM reorganizes NSC to be a resilient national security institution","publisher":"Lawphil / Office of the President","date":"2024-12-30","url":"https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo2024/eo_81_2024.html","summary":"EO 81 reworked the National Security Council into a more coordinated security institution, though still with strong presidential discretion, showing late-year security mobilization.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2"]},{"title":"Philippines: Freedom in the World 2024 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2024","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/philippines/freedom-world/2024","summary":"Freedom House says campaign-finance rules are weak and poorly enforced, and patronage/kinship still shape politics, which means the ruling network was not mobilized through clean, programmatic channels alone.","question_ids":["8B.3","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"Philippines: Freedom on the Net 2024 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2024","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/philippines/freedom-net/2024","summary":"The report says the government and allied actors manipulated online information and retained inherited site blocks, suggesting mobilization relied partly on coercive information control.","question_ids":["8B.3","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"Philippines | Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","date":"2024-06-17","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/digital-news-report/2024/philippines","summary":"Red-tagging, libel pressure, blocked sites, and regulatory pressure on broadcasters persisted, so the state’s mobilization remained partly coercive and not fully rule-bound.","question_ids":["8B.3","7B.9","7B.10"]},{"title":"No PH cooperation with ICC unless PRRD wants it - PBBM","publisher":"Presidential Communications Office","date":"2024-11-14","url":"https://pco.gov.ph/news_releases/no-ph-cooperation-with-icc-unless-prrd-wants-it-pbbm/","summary":"Marcos refused independent ICC cooperation on the Duterte drug war unless Duterte consented, which shows selective accountability and limits on how far he would mobilize the state for external scrutiny.","question_ids":["8B.3","7B.7","7B.10"]},{"title":"NEDA said the rice tariff cut did not reduce retail rice prices as anticipated","publisher":"GMA News Online","date":"2024-12-10","url":"https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/money/economy/929579/neda-reduced-rice-tariffs-failed-to-lower-prices/story/","summary":"The flagship rice intervention only partly worked, showing that some mobilization translated into incomplete execution and weak pass-through.","question_ids":["8B.3","8B.2","7B.5"]},{"title":"TeleRadyo JV with Prime Media / regulatory pressure persists","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","date":"2024-06-17","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/digital-news-report/2024/philippines","summary":"The report notes a Romualdez-linked media joint venture and continued regulatory pressure over broadcasters, suggesting the ruling network still depended on politically connected leverage.","question_ids":["8B.3","7B.9","7B.10"]}]}
